WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:21.111 --> 00:00:22.913
There's a worldwide plastic production

00:00:22.913 --> 00:00:26.350
of 350 million tons a year.

00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:30.387
And about 300 million tons
are ending up as waste.

00:00:35.051 --> 00:00:36.853
We've put billions of tons, actually,

00:00:36.853 --> 00:00:38.662
of plastic into the environment.

00:00:39.025 --> 00:00:41.885
By 2050 people have
predicted that there'll be

00:00:41.885 --> 00:00:45.990
more plastic in the ocean
than fish in terms of weight.

00:00:46.963 --> 00:00:48.157
Remnants of our products

00:00:48.157 --> 00:00:50.608
have spread to every corner of the planet.

00:00:51.006 --> 00:00:53.201
With both global production of plastics

00:00:53.201 --> 00:00:57.882
and the cost of recycling
rising, the outlook is bleak.

00:00:57.958 --> 00:01:01.585
But our planet has a remarkable
way of fighting back.

00:01:01.585 --> 00:01:04.459
Recently discovered
plastic-eating bacteria

00:01:04.459 --> 00:01:06.957
has given scientists hope.

00:01:06.957 --> 00:01:09.026
Hope to decontaminate our planet

00:01:09.026 --> 00:01:11.428
and make cleaner products
for the future.

